allowing degradation  or side reactions to start happening  so the primary seal that we put onto the  cake it can either be done in the freeze  dryer by means of collapsing shelves and  driving bungs into vials  or we can move them into either a  nitrogen box or a dry box  which are held at very low humidities so  under one percent humidity  and then we put a foil seal on  the cakes that then sealed we then pouch  into a desiccated foil pouch  with whatever label is the customer  requires on there  and this step is done in a room that's  held under 35  humidity so if stored in the sealed foil  pouch  then our typical stability is for well  over a year for custom products  so going on to a case study  so earlier on this year we there was a  company called  gene drive who are a point of care  diagnostic company  they came to us and asked us to help to  work with them to develop  a covert test that could be used in  labs around the world  so just going to talk through  in three months we managed to design  develop and then transfer  a covet assay  so for the first stage we sat down and  planned out the project with gene drive  with their requirements that the tests  would be  able to be used in labs worldwide this  meant that it would have to be able to  be used  in multiple different thermal cyclers  now a lot of different thermocyclers  have need different tube types and to  prevent  having to transfer from after they've  reconstituted  the cake or the bead we don't we did not  want to have to transfer  that reconstituted reagent into another  tube to be able to run  so this meant that we would have to  uh this meant that we would have to have  many different plastic wares for this  product  as it was a covered test the forecast  was also very big  and the demand would have been high  because of this we decided on the bead  format  now we the first steps we did were some  initial proof of principle runs in the  dedicated r d facility so at cardiff we  have  two facilities one set up one's  dedicated to r d  and one's dedicated to manufacture both  of which  have the same pretty much the same  equipment but the r d version slightly  smaller  so with gene drive gene drive designed  the  test and centers down the reagents we  lyophilized several different versions  of it sometimes in the same run  sometimes in  different runs took them out the freeze  dryer and sent them back up to gene  drive as quickly as possible  we then sit down and go through the  results with gene drive decide on the  next steps  so after several iterations we came upon  a formulation that we  was fixed we were happy with and we then  looked to transfer this into manufacture  so during the transfer process what we  wanted to do was ensure that we had a  robust product and that  it would we'd be able to manufacture it  day in day out  so we worked with gene drive and decided  that we would run three different  batches  and we'd slowly scale up from an r d  size run  to a manufacture size run now the  the idea of the product with gene drive  is that we would manufacture  one batch of bulk beads and these bulk  beads could be stored at sativa and then  dispensed into the plastic where needed  so there are four different types of  plastic wear depending on which  thermocyclers would need to be used  and we'd be able to use the one bulk one  batch of bulk bees to dispense into any  of these plate types  after we'd run the transfer runs we sat  down again with gene drive and confirmed  that  we were happy with the results they were  happy with the results  and that with the transfer have been  successful and this product was now  launched in manufacture  so currently it's in manufacture the  manufacturing team  run this regularly  and because of the the way the assay has  been designed  when gene drive have discovered that a  further form  plate type is needed then the  then it's a simple case of validating  the new ceiling methods for the plates  but the bog beats remain the same so we  can launch new products quickly  so to summarize gene drive came to us at  the beginning of the year  wanting to develop a cover test we  worked with them to streamline the tests  push it through our systems as quickly  as possible while covering everything  that we needed to cover  and we now have a reliable  and we now have a manufacturing product  which is suitable for  covet tests around the world in many  different thermocyclers  so we've got a couple of places where we  can get more information  there is a video which shows you our  live stable facility and takes you on a  tour around our lab  we've got a couple of papers that are  useful  and we've also got a form to  we also have a form for you to request a  proof of principle run  thank you very much and is there any  questions  thank you amy for the outstanding  presentation we will now move to the  live  q a portion of the presentation as a  reminder to the audience  please submit your questions via the q a  box  so let's take a look it looks like we  already have some great questions  coming in amy our first question  how long does it take for a proof of  principle to be run  so the first thing we'll do is work with  you  to decide on exactly what we want to  test  both what fits you best and what we can  run in one run and after we've decided  that and fully locked down  we will the aim is to have  samples shipping back out to you within  two weeks of receiving  your reagents on site for a standard run  if it's a larger run  and particularly if it's a bead run this  may be a bit longer  but we'll let you know beforehand if it  will be any longer  wonderful thank you and now how many  excipients  do you have so we do have a range of  excipients  we have uh eight standard ones if we  need them  typically we would start off with up to  four  depending on the type of assay we're  lyophilizing  and initially we test them wet and we  try  one or two in the first three first few  proof of principle runs  thank you so much our one audience  member  says i am iso one three four eight five  regulated can you manufacture our  products  yes we can so we are currently iso 9000  9001 regulated in cardiff  uh we are in the process of getting  13485 but we don't have it yet  and we do manufacture many 13485  products  thank you so much now how much does a  proof of principal  run cost so the  uh ethos of the custom team is not to  make any money of the proof of principal  runs  we will we look to cover our costs so  our proof of principal runs start  from as little as 1500 and  they go up depending on what the the  complexity of the pop and the number of  samples needed  thank you and i want to thank our  audience members for these great  questions  our next question is do we have to do  any validation  on ourselves as part of the proof of  principle  so for the proof of principles there  would be no validation that we would  need to do  however after the aim of the proof of  principles is to get a product into  manufacture  and as part of the manufacturing process  what we need to do is scale up so we  need to start  looking at things um like how we  dispense so in the proof of principle  runs we'll be dispensing  30 plates at a maximum properly  thank you so much is it possible  to arrange a site visit to the cardiff  site  yeah um normally um we say yes  at the moment we're doing a lot more  virtual tours so we can give you a  virtual tour of our site and we can do  virtual audits  and we can still welcome visitors if we  need to  um but normally yes it's we're very open  to visits  wonderful thank you we have time for one  more question what is the lead time  amy to secure a gmp run  so it does depend on the complexity of  the project  so and once we've started  once we've done all the proof of  principles and we have a lockdown  formulation  we will then start the transfer runs now  this can take anything from  six weeks to a couple of months or  longer depending on the complexity of  your project  and the urgency of which everything is  needed  and we'll take it through to the core  team so  once we've done the development we then  report our findings to the head of r d  head of manufacturer head of tech  support and between  us and working with yourselves the  customer we will develop  a action plan as to checking out all the  risks that we need  to look at before we can put this into  manufacture  once we've done the design transfer plan  and we've  validated everything that we've agreed  on we will then need to set it up in our  system  so it and so it is manufactured as a  full-on product  so it can be anything from a couple of  months to  a couple to longer depending on  complexity and amy this same audience  member wants to know  is it possible to get a copy of this  slide wheel of services  provided um we could  we have a copy of the information so in  our booth the  accelerating diagnostic development with  custom design services  there is a collection of web links one  of those for the custom  services for genomics is links to a web  page which has all the information that  was in that slide  wonderful amy thank you for your  presentation today and for your  important research  would you like to offer any closing  remarks to our audience before we go  just thank you for listening and if you  have any further questions  and please join me in the booth  amy thank you again amy webster and i  want to thank our audience members for  their participation  any questions that were submitted and  not answered today by our speaker will  be addressed  via email this presentation will be  available for on-demand  viewing for up to 12 months so please  remember to share it with your  colleagues who might be interested in  today's  topic and don't miss out on the other  presentations on our agenda  visit the agenda tab at the auditorium  for a full  listing thank you again for your  participation until next time t